        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "36664e01-a163-5d21-92a3-fa7a1130b5a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Armand Castelmary, Giacomo Meyerbeer, Giuseppe Verdi, Ambroise Thomas, Michel Carré, Jules Barbier, Alexandre Dumas, père, Paul Meurice, William Shakespeare\n- Works: L'Africaine, Don Carlos, Hamlet\n- Organizations: Paris Opera\n- Topics: opera premieres, grand opera, librettos, adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- In 1865, Armand Castelmary created the role of Don Diego in the Paris Opera premiere of Giacomo Meyerbeer's L'Africaine.\n- In 1867, Armand Castelmary created the role of the Monk in the Paris Opera premiere of Giuseppe Verdi's Don Carlos.\n- In 1868, Armand Castelmary created the role of Horatio in the Paris Opera premiere of Ambroise Thomas's Hamlet.\n- Hamlet is a 1868 grand opera in five acts by Ambroise Thomas.\n- The libretto of Hamlet was written by Michel Carré and Jules Barbier.\n- Hamlet is based on a French adaptation by Alexandre Dumas, père, and Paul Meurice of William Shakespeare's play Hamlet.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
